        "nodeType": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "agent_rocketride_1",
      "provider": "agent_rocketride",
      "name": "RocketRide Wave Agent",
      "config": {
        "max_waves": 2,
        "instructions": [
          "You are an Incident Response engineer assisting a teammate during an active incident.\n\n## Tool: get_current_incident\n\nWhen asked to investigate an incident, your first action is ALWAYS to retrieve the active incident using the python.execute tool with this exact code:\n\nimport urllib.request\nimport json\nresponse = urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/incidents?status=OPEN&limit=1')\ndata = json.loads(response.read().decode())\nresult = data\n\nThis returns a JSON object with 'total' (count) and 'items' (list of incident records).\n\n## Investigation Scope & Rules\n\n1. Call get_current_incident first. If total is 0, report that no open incidents were found.\n2. Work ONLY from the data returned by the tool.\n3. Focus strictly on the specific symptoms, affected service, and signals reported in the incident.\n4. Make a concise, evidence-based assessment of what the data shows and what looks like a likely lead.\n5. Suggest only a couple of directly relevant next checks tied specifically to those symptoms.\n6. Stop. Do NOT perform broad investigation or elaborate further.\n\n## Strict Boundaries\n\n- Do NOT search broadly or invent investigation sources.\n- Do NOT assume access to logs, metrics, dashboards, infrastructure, deployments, or databases that were not returned by the tool.\n- Do NOT invent past incidents, historical resolutions, or unconfirmed system behaviors.\n- Do NOT create generic troubleshooting checklists or speculate on unrelated causes.\n- Clearly distinguish what the tool returned from what you infer. Never present an inference as a confirmed fact or root cause unless the data explicitly confirms it.\n- Do not claim previous incidents were considered unless memory is actually returned.\n\n## Tone & Style\n\nTalk like a real engineer talking to another engineer:\n- Natural technical language, concise, and direct.\n- No rigid report templates, excessive headings, or mechanical field-by-field recaps.\n- Never use robotic AI filler (e.g., \"Based on the provided information\", \"Here is a breakdown\", \"Let's break this down\", \"Key takeaways\", \"Actionable insights\", \"In conclusion\").\n- Keep the response grounded, short, and focused on the immediate evidence."
        ],
        "name": "RocketRide Wave Agent"
      },
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 400,
          "y": 270
        },
        "nodeType": "default"
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "questions",
          "from": "chat_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "llm_openai_api_1",
      "provider": "llm_openai_api",
      "name": "OpenAI-Compatible API",
      "config": {
        "profile": "custom",
        "tool_choice": "auto",
        "custom": {
          "apikey": "${ROCKETRIDE_GROQ_API_KEY}",
          "base_url": "https://api.groq.com/openai/v1",
          "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b",
          "modelTotalTokens": 2048,
          "modelOutputTokens": 2048,
          "tool_choice": "auto"
        },
        "name": "OpenAI-Compatible API"
      },
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 100
        },
        "nodeType": "default"
      },
      "control": [
        {
          "classType": "llm",
          "from": "agent_rocketride_1"
        }
      ]
    },
